Carafe bench: a storage buffer whose size Eden guesses stays inside contiguous device memory. The NVN-style
guess takes the GPU range of the same kind from GetMemoryLayoutSize, up to 8 MiB, and the buffer cache then
registers that many bytes as one device-contiguous buffer. NVK's meta copy shaders take storage buffer
addresses from push constants; for nvk-meta-copy-queries at GPU 0x16f9480000 the guess was 0x130000 bytes
while only 0x10000 were contiguous in device memory. The cached buffer covered device pages that NVK later
used for the root descriptor table of a vk-meta-copy-buffer dispatch. DeviceMemoryManager::Map does not
invalidate the cache, so the CPU writes to that table were not seen, the copy ran with stale push constants,
DXVK's shader data buffer stayed zero and its fixed-function draws produced no pixels. The size is now
clamped to MaxContinuousRange. On the hardware the GPU reads memory directly and there is no such cache.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -1924,7 +1924,8 @@ Binding BufferCache<P>::StorageBufferBinding(GPUVAddr ssbo_addr, u32 cbuf_index,
         // Fall through: either not NVN cbuf (Doom Eternal & +), or NVN but ssbo_addr+8 is a GPU address (MCI)
         const u32 memory_layout_size = static_cast<u32>(gpu_memory->GetMemoryLayoutSize(gpu_addr));
         // Cap at 8MB to prevent allocator overflow from misinterpreted addresses
-        return (std::min)(memory_layout_size, static_cast<u32>(8_MiB));
+        const u32 capped_size = (std::min)(memory_layout_size, static_cast<u32>(8_MiB));
+        return static_cast<u32>(gpu_memory->MaxContinuousRange(gpu_addr, capped_size));
     }();
 
     // Alignment only applies to the offset of the buffer
